screen Topics: language grants jobs keys settings errors tour
screen Commands:
screen   bg        continue a stopped job in the background
screen   cat       print files
screen   cd        change the current directory
screen   count     count arguments, or the lines of files
screen   cp        copy a file
screen   date      show the date and time
screen   echo      print its arguments
screen   exit      end this shell; a new one starts
screen   export    give a variable to the programs you run
screen   fetch     fetch a page over HTTP
screen   fg        continue a job in the foreground
screen   find      find files by name
screen   grants    show what a command would be given, without running it
screen   head      print the first lines of files
screen   help      show help
screen   history   list the lines you have run
screen   jobs      list jobs
screen   kill      end a job
screen   ls        list a directory
screen   math      calculate
screen   mkdir     make a directory
prefix -- space: next page, q: quit --
key spc
window
screen   mv        move or rename
screen   net       show the state of the network
screen   ping      send echo requests to a host and show the replies
screen   poweroff  turn the machine off
screen   pwd       print the current directory
screen   random    show random bytes
screen   reboot    start the machine again
screen   rm        remove files
screen   room      list, enter, make or remove rooms
screen   search    find lines that contain text
screen   set       set a variable
screen   settings  show or change settings
screen   sleep     wait for some seconds
screen   slots     list the shell's handles
screen   source    run a script in this shell
screen   stat      describe a file
screen   status    describe how the last command ended
screen   sync      make written data durable
screen   test      check a condition
screen   top       each room's use against its limits
screen   unset     remove a variable
screen   uptime    time since boot
screen   wait      wait for background jobs
prefix -- space: next page, q: quit --
key spc
window
